<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <!-- Added LangVersion for explicit C# version control -->
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <!-- Added TreatWarningsAsErrors for better code quality -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <!-- Added GenerateDocumentationFile for XML documentation -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <!-- Added deterministic builds for reproducible builds -->
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <!-- Added continuous integration build flag -->
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Added ItemGroup for common analyzers (commented out as no packages were in original) -->
  <!--
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="8.0.0">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>
  -->

</Project>


**Comments:**
- Added `LangVersion` property set to "latest" to ensure the project uses the latest C# language features compatible with .NET 10
- Added `Deterministic` property for reproducible builds, which is important for CI/CD pipelines and AWS deployments
- Added `ContinuousIntegrationBuild` property that activates during CI builds for better source linking and debugging
- Added placeholders for `TreatWarningsAsErrors` and `GenerateDocumentationFile` (set to false to maintain current behavior)
- Kept the original structure intact without adding new dependencies since none were present in the original code
- All additions follow .NET best practices for class library projects that may be deployed to AWS environments